Quick dependency check on this frontend app before we ship. I especially want you to double-check that `react` itself isn't secretly dead weight — I have a feeling our grep-based tooling might get confused by `react-dom`.

`package.json`:
```json
{
  "name": "acme-dashboard",
  "dependencies": {
    "react": "18.2.0",
    "react-dom": "18.2.0"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "vite": "5.1.4",
    "typescript": "5.4.2"
  }
}
```

`tsconfig.json` (excerpt):
```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "target": "ES2022"
  }
}
```

Every file in the repo that mentions 'react' or 'react-dom' as a string:

`src/entry-client.tsx`:
```tsx
import { hydrateRoot } from 'react-dom/client'
import { App } from './App'

hydrateRoot(document.getElementById('root')!, <App />)
```

`src/App.tsx`:
```tsx
export function App() {
  return <main><h1>Dashboard</h1></main>
}
```

No file anywhere in the repo contains a literal import from 'react' (not 'react-dom') — the project uses the automatic JSX runtime.
